    "chunk_text": "wxl 2134$50 - 2019 wf.daia;= ui 02 jeks isl=rdod - 2019'08'02\n\nNo. 2134/50 \u2013 FRIDAY, AUGUST 02, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I: SECTION (I) - GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nBOTANIC GARDENS ORDINANCE \u2013No. 31 of 1928\n\nREGULATIONS made by the Minister of Tourism Development, Wild Life and Christianity Religious Affairs under\n\nparagraph (c) of sub section (1) of Section (3) of the Botanic Gardens Ordinance No.31 of 1928 amended by Act, No.32 of\n\n1973.\n\nJOHN AMARATUNGA,Minister of Tourism Development,\n\nWild Life and Christianity Religious Affairs.Colombo,\n\n06th of June, 2019.\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\n1A - G30652- 67 (08/2019)\n\nI fldgi: (I) fPaoh - Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'02PART I:SEC.(I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 02.08.2019\n\n1.These regulations are called as Botanic Gardens (Admission Fees) of 2019 and shall be implemented with effectfrom 05th August, 2019.\n\n2.The amount of the fees levied to enter person and vehicles to any Botanic Gardens shall be as mentioned in theschedule here.Even though the below mentioned persons will be exempted from paying this entrance fee :\n\nA.Visitors of Sri Lankan RepublicB.Dwellers of the residences within the gardens.\n\nC.Government servants who enter into the gardens for official duties.D.Person who are granted free admission to the Director General.\n\nProvided further in relation to the Botanic Gardens where the vehicles are not permitted, no vehicle otherthan vehicles permitted by curator of Botanic Gardens shall be permitted to enter such Botanic Gardens.\n\n3.The admission to Botanic Gardens Regulation published to Gazette Extraordinary No.1685/17 of 22.12.2010and amended by the GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY No.1700/10 of 06.04.2011 & by the Gazette Extraordinary No.1969 of"
