    "chunk_size_bytes": 1769,
    "chunk_text": "4. Every operator shall submit to the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka (hereinafter referredto as the \u201cTRCSL\u201d) the details of the procedure complied by such operator for the purpose of implementing themeasures set out in such Schedule I and II hereto.\n\n6. For the purpose of these regulations -\n\n\u201cAct\u201d means the Sri Lanka Telecommunications Act, No. 25 of 1991 ;\n\n\u201ccorporate subscriber\u201d means any person under whose company name, SIM cards are registered by theoperators for the use of its employees, agents or any other authorized person ;\n\n\u201cperson\u201d means a body incorporated or unincorporated ;\n\n\u201cretail subscriber\u201d means any person under whose personal name, SIM Card is registered by theoperators ;\n\n\u201cSIM\u201d means the Subscriber Identification Modules ;\n\n\u201cSIM Card\u201d means the card or the chip issued to a subscriber containing the Subscriber IdentificationModules.\n\n(Regulation 2)\n\nSCHEDULE I\n\nREGISTRATION OF RETAIL SUBSCRIBERS\n\nEvery operator shall comply with the following regulatory measures when registering retail subscriber SIM cards.\n\n1. Obtain a duly filled and signed application form from the retail subscriber. (Mandatory details required : NationalIdentity Card Number, permanent address, new telephone number)\n\n2. The application referred to in paragraph 1 shall accompany the following :\u2013\n\n(a) a photocopy of the National Identity Card or Driving License or Valid Passport duly signed by thesubscriber ;\n\n(b) a duly signed photograph of the retail subscriber with his or her signature where the photograph of theretail subscriber in the National Identity Card or Driving License or Passport is not clear ;\n\n3.(a) the address in the National Identity Card shall be considered as the permanent address."
